WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.347
Paint, press, lift.

2
00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:03.689
A print is a mark you make by pressing.

3
00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:05.614
Put a little paint on a stamp.

4
00:00:05.774 --> 00:00:07.214
Press it straight down.

5
00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.767
Lift it straight up.

6
00:00:08.927 --> 00:00:10.970
The mark that is left is a print.

7
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.785
The same again.

8
00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.685
The best thing about a print is that you can make it again.

9
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:18.306
Press the same stamp, and you get the same mark.

10
00:00:18.466 --> 00:00:22.646
Take turns with two stamps, again and again, and you have a pattern.

11
00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:24.646
Print with anything.

12
00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:26.478
You do not need a shop stamp.

13
00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:27.985
A leaf prints its lines.

14
00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:29.909
A sponge prints tiny dots.

15
00:00:30.069 --> 00:00:31.834
A bottle top prints a circle.

16
00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:34.363
Look at the bumpy side and guess what it will print.

17
00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:36.270
Printed cloth.

18
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:42.189
In Ghana, people print adinkra cloth with stamps carved from a calabash, a hard fruit shell.

19
00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:46.064
They press each stamp again and again, in squares drawn with a comb.

20
00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:48.592
A whole cloth, from just a few stamps.
